# Expectations
The paper’s experiments include an “ADVI (Fisher)” baseline, which is ADVI modified to use the Fisher divergence instead of the ELBO loss. Section 5.1 reports experiments on Gaussian targets with dimensions \(D \in \{4,16,64,256\}\), with results averaged over multiple runs (10 runs, based on Figure 5.1). The current criterion requires actual code that can run **10 separate seeded runs of ADVI (Fisher)** on a \(D\)-dimensional Gaussian target over some number of iterations.

I would expect to find:
- an implementation of ADVI (Fisher), i.e., a stochastic gradient-based variational inference loop using the Fisher divergence as the objective;
- support for Gaussian target distributions of dimension \(D\);
- a mechanism for setting random seeds and running the algorithm independently for 10 seeded runs;
- code that runs enough iterations and stores/returns results from each run;
- actual source files or notebooks containing this implementation, not merely descriptions or instructions.

# Reality
The submission attempt does not provide any files in the `<files>` section; it is empty. Therefore, there are no source files, no implementation code, no scripts, and no logs for me to inspect.

Because no code is included, I cannot verify:
- whether ADVI (Fisher) is implemented;
- whether it can estimate a Gaussian posterior in dimension \(D\);
- whether 10 separate seeded runs can be executed;
- whether iteration results are collected.

The absence of all files means the attempt has not demonstrated the required code.

